        "## From MaxDiff Data to MNL Choices\n",
        "\n",
        "For the MNL model, each class gets a utility coefficient, $\\beta_j$. A higher coefficient means the class is more preferred.\n",
        "\n",
        "For a task showing four classes, the probability that class $j$ is chosen as best is:\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\n",
        "P(\\text{best}=j) = \\frac{\\exp(\\beta_j)}{\\sum_{k \\in \\text{shown}} \\exp(\\beta_k)}\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        "After the best item is chosen, the worst item is modeled from the remaining three classes using flipped utility. A high-utility item should be unlikely to be chosen as worst, so the worst-choice probability uses $-\\beta_j$:\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\n",
        "P(\\text{worst}=j \\mid \\text{best chosen}) = \\frac{\\exp(-\\beta_j)}{\\sum_{k \\in \\text{shown except best}} \\exp(-\\beta_k)}\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        "One technical issue is identification. Adding the same constant to every $\\beta$ does not change the choice probabilities. To solve this, I set item 1 as the reference class with $\\beta_1 = 0$ and estimate the other nine coefficients."
      ],
      "id": "1086211d"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "#| label: likelihood-functions\n",
        "\n",
        "K = J - 1  # estimate beta_2 through beta_10; beta_1 is fixed at 0\n",
        "\n",
        "def full_beta(beta_free):\n",
        "    \"\"\"Insert reference beta_1 = 0.\"\"\"\n",
        "    return np.r_[0.0, np.asarray(beta_free)]\n",
        "\n",
        "def log_likelihood(beta_free):\n",
        "    \"\"\"Vectorized MaxDiff log-likelihood.\"\"\"\n",
        "    beta = full_beta(beta_free)\n",
        "    v = beta[shown_mat]  # n_tasks x 4\n",
        "\n",
        "    best_part = beta[best_idx] - logsumexp(v, axis=1)\n",
        "\n",
        "    # For the worst choice, remove the item already picked as best.\n",
        "    remaining_mask = shown_mat != best_idx[:, None]\n",
        "    neg_v_remaining = np.where(remaining_mask, -v, -np.inf)\n",
        "    worst_part = -beta[worst_idx] - logsumexp(neg_v_remaining, axis=1)\n",
        "\n",
        "    return float(np.sum(best_part + worst_part))\n",
        "\n",
        "def neg_log_likelihood(beta_free):\n",
        "    return -log_likelihood(beta_free)\n",
        "\n",
        "def log_likelihood_grad(beta_free):\n",
        "    \"\"\"Gradient of the log-likelihood for beta_2 through beta_10.\"\"\"\n",
        "    beta = full_beta(beta_free)\n",
        "    v = beta[shown_mat]\n",
        "\n",
        "    # Best choice contribution: chosen best minus softmax over shown items.\n",
        "    p_best = np.exp(v - logsumexp(v, axis=1, keepdims=True))\n",
        "    grad = np.zeros(J)\n",
        "    np.add.at(grad, best_idx, 1.0)\n",
        "    for col in range(shown_mat.shape[1]):\n",
        "        np.add.at(grad, shown_mat[:, col], -p_best[:, col])\n",
        "\n",
        "    # Worst choice contribution: chosen worst gets -1; remaining items get softmax over -utility.\n",
        "    remaining_mask = shown_mat != best_idx[:, None]\n",
        "    neg_v_remaining = np.where(remaining_mask, -v, -np.inf)\n",
        "    p_worst = np.exp(neg_v_remaining - logsumexp(neg_v_remaining, axis=1, keepdims=True))\n",
        "    np.add.at(grad, worst_idx, -1.0)\n",
        "    for col in range(shown_mat.shape[1]):\n",
        "        np.add.at(grad, shown_mat[:, col], p_worst[:, col])\n",
        "\n",
        "    return grad[1:]\n",
        "\n",
        "def neg_log_likelihood_grad(beta_free):\n",
        "    return -log_likelihood_grad(beta_free)\n",
        "\n",
        "# Small check: the likelihood at zero is finite.\n",
        "log_likelihood(np.zeros(K))"
      ],
      "id": "likelihood-functions",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
