      "source": [
        "## MNL via Bayesian Estimation\n",
        "\n",
        "The Bayesian model uses the same MNL likelihood, but adds a prior distribution on the coefficients. I use a weakly informative normal prior:\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\\boldsymbol{\\beta} \\sim N(0, 10I)\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        "This prior is wide enough to let the data drive the result, but it also prevents absurdly large estimates. I estimate the posterior distribution using a random-walk Metropolis-Hastings sampler."
      ],
      "id": "bb4bdfce"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "#| label: bayes-functions\n",
        "\n",
        "prior_sd = np.sqrt(10)\n",
        "\n",
        "def log_prior(beta_free):\n",
        "    return np.sum(-0.5 * (beta_free / prior_sd) ** 2 - np.log(prior_sd * np.sqrt(2 * np.pi)))\n",
        "\n",
        "def log_posterior(beta_free):\n",
        "    return log_likelihood(beta_free) + log_prior(beta_free)\n",
        "\n",
        "def mh_sampler(beta0, n_iter=15000, step=0.18):\n",
        "    beta = np.asarray(beta0).copy()\n",
        "    draws = np.zeros((n_iter, len(beta)))\n",
        "    lp = log_posterior(beta)\n",
        "    accept = 0\n",
        "    for t in range(n_iter):\n",
        "        beta_star = beta + np.random.normal(0, step, size=len(beta))\n",
        "        lp_star = log_posterior(beta_star)\n",
        "        if np.log(np.random.rand()) < lp_star - lp:\n",
        "            beta = beta_star\n",
        "            lp = lp_star\n",
        "            accept += 1\n",
        "        draws[t, :] = beta\n",
        "    return draws, accept / n_iter"
      ],
      "id": "bayes-functions",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "#| label: bayes-fit\n",
        "\n",
        "# Starting at the MLE helps the chain settle quickly.\n",
        "draws_free, accept_rate = mh_sampler(beta_mle_free, n_iter=8000, step=0.18)\n",
        "burn = int(0.25 * len(draws_free))\n",
        "post_free = draws_free[burn:, :]\n",
        "post_full = np.column_stack([np.zeros(len(post_free)), post_free])\n",
        "\n",
        "accept_rate"
      ],
      "id": "bayes-fit",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
